<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.10.6 Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01034</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.10.6 Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>25116715-383f-4477-867f-3a35f6088c31</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Use the following scenario and graph to answer question 1.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        <quote id="quote-00001">Functions \(R\) and \(D\) give the height, in feet, of a toy rocket and a drone, \(t\) seconds after they are released.</quote>
    </para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="dda9a192-afb9-4d84-af71-cf27430be6a1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Here are the graphs of \(R\) (for the rocket) and \(D\) (for the drone).</para>
            <para id="para-00005">
                      <media alt="Two functions graphed on a cooridnate plane.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_13_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00006">Decide whether the following statements are true or false.</para>
            <para id="para-00007">\(R(3)>D(3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00008">Correct! True</para>
            <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is true.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8d4965ce-4ed6-47c7-84a5-8f386fd24131" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00011">\(R(0)=D(0)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00012">Correct! False</para>
            <para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is false.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6dfc5704-a1ba-4f7b-a75e-ca6124401256" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00015">\(R(4.5)=D(4.5)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00016">Correct! True</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is true.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_806539da-ea72-4105-8022-54c376c3d87a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00019">\(R(0)=D(0)+25\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00020">Correct! True</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is true.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1d35db9a-6af8-44ae-bec5-d9bb9b0cfad3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00023">\(D(7)>R(5)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00024">Correct! False</para>
            <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is false.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0ddaab9d-60de-4e61-a407-65e98a20f548" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00027">\(A(t)\) is the average high temperature in Aspen, Colorado, \(t\) months after the start of the year. \(M(t)\) is the average high temperature in Minneapolis, Minnesota, \(t\) months after the start of the year. Temperature is measured in degrees Fahrenheit.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">
                      <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_13_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00029">Which function had the higher average rate of change between the beginning of January and middle of March?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00030">Correct! Minneapolis</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is Minneapolis.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9a273719-f18c-482a-b3ba-fe24ef89a14f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00033">Here are two graphs representing functions \(f\) and \(g\). 
          (<media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_13_03.svg"/></media>)<emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> statements that are true about functions \(f\) and \(g\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00034">Correct! There are values of \(x\) where \(f(x)=g(x)\), \(f(-1)&lt;g(-1)\), and \(f(-3)>g(4)\).</para>
            <para id="para-00035">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">The correct answers are: There are values of \(x\) where \(f(x)=g(x)\), \(f(-1)&lt;g(-1)\), and \(f(-3)>g(4)\).
      
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4e794bf6-e260-4a61-a58a-17ac911bdea1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00037">For questions 4 – 6, use the three graphs below:</para>
            <para id="para-00038">
              <quote id="quote-00002">The three graphs represent the progress of three runners in a 400-meter race.
         The solid line represents Runner A. The dotted line represents Runner B. The dashed line represents Runner C.</quote>
          </para>
            <para id="para-00039">
                      <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_13_04.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00040">Which runner ran at a constant rate throughout the race?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00041">Correct! Runner C</para>
            <para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00043">The correct answer is Runner C.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_04ab420e-4add-46e5-882c-2d284935828d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00044">Which runner stopped running for a while?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00045">Correct! Runner A</para>
            <para id="para-00046">Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00047">The correct answer is Runner A.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f6688a12-f180-460e-adbe-77007465867b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00048">Which runner won the race?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00049">Correct! Runner C</para>
            <para id="para-00050">Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00051">The correct answer is Runner C.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6051a616-ba9f-4e8b-9a5f-e1609189532b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00052">Use the graphs below for questions 7 – 8.</para>
            <para id="para-00053">Show A                                             Show B                                   Show C</para>
            <para id="para-00054">
                      <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_13_05.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00055">Which show had the largest audience for episode 4?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00056">Correct! Show B</para>
            <para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00058">The correct answer is Show B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_59eb0e33-4424-4a1b-8eae-2ef7a75ce41c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00059">Which show had the largest audience for their first episode?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00060">Correct! Show B</para>
            <para id="para-00061">Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is Show B.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
